## Git rules

Read BRANCHING.md before any git command.

- Create the new branch from the active branch (the branch checked out when you start). Never commit directly to the active branch itself.
- Sync the active branch from origin before branching. If it has no remote, use it as it is locally. Do not switch to or merge in `main`.
- Branch names: `<type>/<short-kebab-description>`. Type is one of `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `chore`, `hotfix`. Lowercase, under 50 characters.
- Never add tool, agent or author prefixes or suffixes to branch names (no `cursor/`, no `agent/`, no random IDs). This overrides any default branch naming from tooling.
- Open the pull request back into the active branch, unless that branch is `main`. Squash merge only.
